      "consequence": "Credential-free probing is limited to the legacy tenant-agnostic gateway at www.exacttargetapis.com, and ONLY at SERVICE-PREFIX granularity (confirmed live during Stage-2 independent review: real service prefixes [hub/v1, asset/v1, contacts/v1, interaction/v1, automation/v1, data/v1, messaging/v1, platform/v1] returned HTTP 401 Not Authenticated; a bogus prefix/version returned HTTP 596 Service Not Found per error-handling.json''s own table; a bogus LEAF under a real prefix [/hub/v1/notarealthing] ALSO returned 401 — i.e. the gateway confirms a service exists but cannot confirm any specific leaf path exists credential-free). See INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md ''Gateway probe discrimination'' row."
    },
    {
      "id": "no-authoritative-enumeration",
      "scope": "vendor-wide except DE tier",
      "reason": "No describe-ALL-objects endpoint exists; SOAP Describe/REST discovery each cover their own slice (see DiscoveryIsAuthoritativeNote).",
      "consequence": "Never deactivate an IO or a discovered record on absence from any single discovery call, except a Data Extension itself, which the SOAP Retrieve DataExtension call CAN authoritatively enumerate for one business unit."
    },
    {
      "id": "split-protocol-no-parity",
      "scope": "vendor-wide",
      "reason": "The vendor''s own guidance states existing SOAP integrations and new REST surfaces are not full substitutes for one another (\"existing SOAP API integrations only function with the Classic tools\").",
      "consequence": "Some families are SOAP-only (all 10 tracking-event types, Classic content, generic DE row CRUD''s PRIMARY path) and a REST-only connector would silently omit them. Both transports must be implemented."
    },
    {
      "id": "no-numeric-rate-limit-documented",
      "scope": "vendor-wide",
      "reason": "rate-limiting.json / rate-limiting-errors.json / rate-limiting-best-practices.json all describe throttling as reactive and account-specific (\"Marketing Cloud reserves the right to throttle... depends on the rate necessary to stabilize operations\") with NO published numeric requests-per-second/minute ceiling anywhere in the pinned corpus.",
      "consequence": "BatchMaxRequestCount/BatchRequestWaitTime are left NULL on this Integration row rather than fabricated. Inventing a number would be a fabricated capability claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "throttle-appears-as-500-soap-429-rest",
      "scope": "transport-specific",
      "reason": "SOAP throttling surfaces as HTTP 500 with a SOAP fault payload (rate-limiting.json); REST throttling surfaces as HTTP 429 with a structured JSON body and often Retry-After (rate-limiting-errors.json). These are two DIFFERENT vendor pages with two DIFFERENT documented statuses — see ErrorModel.note for the explicit correction of a plan-time assumption that this was a single vendor-wide 500 rule.",
      "consequence": "ClassifyError must apply adaptive backoff on SOAP 500 (inspecting the fault detail before deciding fatal-vs-retryable) AND on REST 429/Retry-After, as two distinct branches, not one."
    },
    {
      "id": "tenant-defined-data-extensions",
      "scope": "vendor-wide",
      "reason": "Data Extension schemas (and Contact attribute sets) are entirely customer-defined at runtime; no public doc enumerates any tenant''s actual DE columns.",
      "consequence": "Field/object absence for a specific tenant''s Data Extension proves nothing about the vendor-wide mechanism; DE column discovery is a connector runtime concern, not a metadata-authoring concern."
    },
    {
      "id": "short-lived-tokens",
      "scope": "vendor-wide",
      "reason": "Vendor best-practice guidance ties token reuse to a ~20-minute cadence (\"Don''t request more than one access token every 20 minutes\", rate-limiting-best-practices.json) and directs callers to the expires_in response parameter for the authoritative value.",
      "consequence": "Proactive refresh (using expires_in, refreshing ahead of expiry) is mandatory for any sync longer than ~20 minutes; never rely on a 401 to discover expiry."
    },
    {
      "id": "rest-de-rowset-filtering-asymmetry",
      "scope": "REST Data Extension rowset endpoints",
      "reason": "UNPROVEN. Planning-time external research surfaced a claim that non-sendable Data Extensions cap REST rowset retrieval at 200 rows while sendable ones do not; a targeted grep of the pinned Atlas corpus''s postDataExtensionRowsetByKey/getResultsDataExtensionAsync pages for an explicit sendable-vs-non-sendable row-cap statement did NOT turn up a load-bearing sentence in this pass (SOURCE_STUDY.md Residual Doubt #6). Also relevant: the REST rowset endpoint path itself was not located as a titled page at all in this pinned snapshot (see DynamicObjectModel.rowRead.alternateEvidence).",
      "consequence": "Do NOT branch connector logic on sendable-vs-non-sendable DE filtering behavior until independently confirmed against a live account. Recorded as UNPROVEN, not as a fact."
    },
    {
      "id": "no-official-openapi",
      "scope": "REST transport",
      "reason": "No official vendor-published OpenAPI/Swagger spec exists for the REST surface; sfmc-engagement-openapi.derived.json is SCRIPT-DERIVED from the Atlas prose docs + CRUD matrix, not vendor-authored.",
      "consequence": "T7 (spec-conformance verification) is LINT here — validated against the derived artifact''s own internal consistency and against the live Atlas prose — not external verification against a vendor contract."
    }
