  "APIVersioningStrategy": "url-path",
  "APIVersioningStrategyNote": "URL-path segment, but NOT globally uniform: all REST resource-family paths observed carry /v1/ immediately after the service prefix (hub/v1, asset/v1, contacts/v1, interaction/v1, automation/v1, data/v1, messaging/v1, platform/v1, sms/v1, push/v1 — 10 distinct service prefixes observed across sources/rest-parsed.json). The Auth service specifically uses /v2/ (v2/token, v2/userinfo, v2/discovery, routes.json) — a different version number under a different service. Do not assume a single vendor-wide version constant.",
  "CustomObjectMarkerPattern": null,
  "CustomObjectMarkerPatternGap": "No naming-convention marker for custom objects was located. Unlike e.g. HubSpot''s p_<accountID>_<name>, SFMC''s customer-custom-object mechanism (Data Extensions) has no distinguishing name prefix — a Data Extension IS the custom-object primitive itself, not a marked subset of a larger object catalog. Left NULL; see DynamicObjectModel for the actual mechanism.",
  "CustomFieldMarkerPattern": null,
  "CustomFieldMarkerPatternGap": "No naming-convention marker for custom fields was located in the pinned corpus. Left NULL.",
